  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district, governmental funds only (no enterprise funds; School Nutrition is a nonmajor governmental fund here). Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (pp4-6); transfers in/out 84,033 each are interfund within governmental funds, shown after the totals. Balance sheet uses the net position section of the Statement of Activities and Net Position (p3); no liabilities. Debt service 278,208 split into principal 240,493 and interest 37,715 per the Special Building Fund schedule (p15). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (pp10-12) used for the General Fund; the General Fund Components combining schedule (pp8-9) is not recorded to avoid double counting (its reclassification column moves State categorical 693,744 and Federal programs 445,523 into Regular instruction 1,047,158 and Special education 92,109; the 75,000 General Fund transfer is shown in disbursements there but is a transfer on the statement and is recorded as other financing). Transfer cross-check: General transfer out 75,000 = SNP 41,000 + Co-op 34,000 in; Bond Fund transfer out 9,033 = General transfers in 9,033; Depreciation Fund budgeted transfer 150,000 had no actual. Budget lines with blank actuals (e.g. tuition 1323, other local receipts 1990, other support services 2900, Employee Benefit nonprogram receipts/benefits paid, QCPUF building and sites) are omitted. Statement header on pp4-7 prints 'August 21, 2025' for the governmental funds statement, treated as a typo for August 31. Read pages 1-19 of 19"
}